\series bold
Exercise 5.8
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Find the ground state of the system from Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:DrivenBinaryWireN2"

\end_inset

 under the simplifications 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta\rightarrow0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\gamma\rightarrow0$
\end_inset

.
 You may assume 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{k}>0$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
#+html:
 <details><summary>Show/hide solution...</summary>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Here,
 the Hamiltonian assumes a diagonal form:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{H}\rightarrow\left[\begin{array}{cccc}
\frac{E_{k}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\
0 & -\frac{E_{k}}{2} & 0 & 0\\
0 & 0 & -\frac{E_{k}}{2} & 0\\
0 & 0 & 0 & \frac{E_{k}}{2}
\end{array}\right]
\]

\end_inset

Because of this,
 we can know that the eigenvalues and eigenvectors are:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
-\frac{E_{k}}{2}\quad\text{for}\quad\ket{01},\ket{10}
\]

\end_inset

and
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\frac{E_{k}}{2}\quad\text{for}\quad\ket{11},\ket{00}.
\]

\end_inset

Because the lowest-energy eigenvalue 
\begin_inset Formula $-E_{k}/2$
\end_inset

 (the ground state energy) appears twice,
 the system is said to be doubly degenerate,
 any linear combination of states
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
c_{01}\ket{01}+c_{10}\ket{10}
\]

\end_inset

has the same (minimum) energy as the ground state.
 It is customary to pick a combination of states as the ground state:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\ket{\psi_{0}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\ket{10}+\ket{01}\right).
\]

\end_inset

